# How Light Bounces: a teaching film for one technique of ray tracing - global illumination, light that bounces from surface to surface - shown side by side.
# Every frame is rendered twice from the same camera, each half the whole view (`sidebyside depth 1`): on the left the rays stop at the first surface they meet, so a
# surface is lit only by what reaches it straight from the sun or the sky; on the right the light bounces as many times as the video's ray depth allows.
# The set is the Sun Hall (film_assets/how-light-bounces/sun_hall.pbrt, written by scripts/lessons/sun_hall.py): an original domed marble rotunda whose only light is the
# sun through the oculus at its crown - one bright disc on the far wall, and everything else lit by the light that disc gives back. Its captions: film_assets/
# how-light-bounces/captions.txt. Render it at a ray depth of 8 or more (the app's Max depth) to see the right half at its best.
film    how-light-bounces
name    How Light Bounces
about   A teaching film: a marble hall lit only by the sun through its dome, shown twice side by side - with light that stops at the first surface, and with light that bounces.
scene   film_assets/how-light-bounces/sun_hall.pbrt
length  30
tags    teaching, lighting, indoors

sidebyside depth 1
music      clear

# one move through the hall: low by the entrance facing the sunlit wall, round to the right past the gold sphere, up past the columns, a look up into the dome and
# its oculus, and down again to look back across the hall
shot 0 The Sun Hall
  key    0 1.8 15     0 7 -12     65
  key    9 2.6 9     -6 8 -9      65
  key   12 6 -1      -8 13 2      70
  key    4 9 -6       0 32 1      82
  key   -9 2.2 -7     8 3.5 5     58
